Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns / potential usage  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ToUserId": id of the user who receives each up‑vote (count them to know how many up‑votes a user received).  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."FromUserId": id of the user who casts each up‑vote (count them to know how many up‑votes a user gave).  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."Id": the vote record itself; counting distinct "Id" gives the number of distinct up‑votes.  
• USERS."Id": primary key, to be matched with "ToUserId" / "FromUserId".  
• USERS."UserName": the screen name we need to show in result.  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
– "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL  (ignore system / deleted rows)  
– "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL  
– Filter or order with COUNT(*) DESC to obtain the leaders.  

Below are 10 exploratory → final Snowflake SQL queries (all SELECT‑only, each capped by LIMIT 20 rows) designed to understand the data and culminate in the query that answers the task.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a handful of raw vote rows.
SELECT *
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show votes where a recipient (“ToUserId”) exists.
SELECT "Id", "ForumMessageId", "FromUserId", "ToUserId", "VoteDate"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) How many distinct up‑votes has each user received?
SELECT "ToUserId",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "received_votes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "ToUserId"
ORDER BY "received_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) How many distinct up‑votes has each user given?
SELECT "FromUserId",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "given_votes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "FromUserId"
ORDER BY "given_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Attach usernames to the top vote recipients.
SELECT u."UserName",
       r."received_votes"
FROM (
    SELECT "ToUserId", COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "received_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "ToUserId"
    ORDER BY "received_votes" DESC
    LIMIT 20
) r
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" u
  ON u."Id" = r."ToUserId"
ORDER BY r."received_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Attach usernames to the top vote givers.
SELECT u."UserName",
       g."given_votes"
FROM (
    SELECT "FromUserId", COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "given_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId"
    ORDER BY "given_votes" DESC
    LIMIT 20
) g
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" u
  ON u."Id" = g."FromUserId"
ORDER BY g."given_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Build an all‑users table of votes‑received counts.
SELECT u."Id"            AS "UserId",
       u."UserName",
       COUNT(DISTINCT v."Id") AS "received_votes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS"               u
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
       ON v."ToUserId" = u."Id"
GROUP BY u."Id", u."UserName"
ORDER BY "received_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Build an all‑users table of votes‑given counts.
SELECT u."Id"            AS "UserId",
       u."UserName",
       COUNT(DISTINCT v."Id") AS "given_votes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS"               u
LEFT JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
       ON v."FromUserId" = u."Id"
GROUP BY u."Id", u."UserName"
ORDER BY "given_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Combine received and given counts in one view for the top 10 receivers.
WITH r AS (
    SELECT "ToUserId" AS "UserId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "received_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "ToUserId"
),
g AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "given_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId"
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       COALESCE(r."received_votes", 0) AS "received_votes",
       COALESCE(g."given_votes",   0) AS "given_votes"
FROM r
LEFT JOIN g ON g."UserId" = r."UserId"
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" u ON u."Id" = r."UserId"
ORDER BY r."received_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL QUERY – return the top three users with the most distinct up‑votes received,
--                plus how many distinct up‑votes they have given.
WITH received AS (
    SELECT "ToUserId"  AS "UserId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "received_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "ToUserId"
),
given AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "given_votes"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId"
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       r."received_votes",
       COALESCE(g."given_votes", 0) AS "given_votes"
FROM received r
LEFT JOIN given g ON g."UserId" = r."UserId"
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" u ON u."Id" = r."UserId"
ORDER BY r."received_votes" DESC
LIMIT 3;
```
